      "message": "fix(slot): pin the fit tolerances and refusals; inscribe a chorded face\n\nReview of PR #1522:\n- Near-miss pins for FIT_TOL and STRAIGHT_TOL on the edge and the face\n  room (0.02 mm out refused, 0.005 mm out taken).\n- A pin for every refusal: the face's wall and end laws, the selection\n  shapes of slot_bound_of, from_face no area, fit no width, from_edges\n  no length, confine's finite/positive guard, and CreateOperation's\n  seed with its undo.\n- A tessellated round-ended face is inscribed: the fitted slot's radius\n  is drawn in by the measured chord sag (up to 5% of the width), never\n  the tolerance loosened. A face that still seeds nothing says why in\n  the refusal (SlotBound::judge) instead of a bare length refusal.\n- face_overshoot is exact: region edges against the slot's centre\n  segment (segment distance) plus the end centres' containment, in\n  place of 0.5 mm boundary sampling.\n\nRefs #1504\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
