      "message": "test(slot): pin the face law's segment-crossing branch; say the inscribe cap is per side\n\nReview of #1522 (b1e25d27): deleting the crossing branch of\n`seg_seg_dist` stayed green - a thin wall across the slot, every\nvertex farther than r from the centre line, was accepted. The\nreviewer's slit-hole face now pins it (\"runs 3.000 mm outside the\npicked face\"); with the branch removed it goes red.\n\nThe INSCRIBE_MAX doc and the decision said a 5% width shrink; the code\ncaps the draw-in per side (up to 10% of the width). Both now say so.\n\nRefs #1504\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
